From dd541e937ae195daf70ab4e156fe111d648407e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 17:46:18 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 88/99] dialog: Asks before "Kill", as Window Maker's message
 dialog.

"Kill" in the menu of the Dock's, the Clip's and the dock-apps' tiles
asks first, as Window Maker does ("Kill Application": "<name> will be
forcibly closed. Any unsaved changes will be lost. Please confirm.").

The dialog is a window of the compositor, laid out as wMessageDialog: The
logo (the Dock's main tile icon), the title in large letters, an engraved
separator, the message, and the buttons at the lower right, the default
one with the return arrow. Drawn with the menu's style. Return or the
default button confirms; Escape, the other button or closing declines.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
